	"notes": "Vercel's homepage pairs a short, punchy headline on the left with a three-line feature list floating far to the right, separated by a lot of empty space — an unusual choice, since most two-column heroes put the second block right next to the first. On a laptop and up, the whole page is capped at 1448 pixels and centres itself, so an ultrawide monitor just gets wider margins, not a wider page — a pattern several other sites in this set also use. On a phone the page does not stack that floating list underneath the headline the way a normal sidebar would; it just removes it entirely, so the phone version is shorter on purpose, not because something failed to reflow.",
